-- title:
--   Integral closedness of K ⊗_ℤ_{(ℓ)} chartAlgFin in characteristic zero
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) $\ell$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure and finite-dimensional as a $\mathbb{Q}$-vector space. Let $A =$ `chartAlgFin` $N\ \ell$ be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull` $N$ whose elements are exactly those integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by the single element `jFull` $N$ (the modular function $j$ viewed inside that field); thus $A$ is the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ in the full modular function field of level $N$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions about the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra tensor product $K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$: it is a domain (a nontrivial commutative ring without zero divisors), and it is integrally closed, in the sense that every element of its fraction field integral over it already lies in the image of the ring.
--
--   This is the statement that the $j$-finite chart of the Igusa model at level $N$ stays an integrally closed domain after base change from $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ to any number field $K$, the constant-field extension case of the ascent of normality along separable base change. It is used in the construction of the affine charts of [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) over such $K$, namely by [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algEquiv_tensor_chartAlgFin_mul_chartAlgFin_laurentBaseChange_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algEquiv_tensor_chartAlgFin_mul_chartAlgFin_laurentBaseChange_of_not_dvd) and by [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algHom_tensor_chartAlg_injective_isIntegrallyClosed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algHom_tensor_chartAlg_injective_isIntegrallyClosed).
